@startuml Kaigara-Architecture
title Kaigara -- System Architecture\n(Option C: the EngineAdapter seam is in place; only the k6 adapter is implemented -- ADR 0001.\nThe adapter compiles the timeline itself; no plan crosses the seam -- ADR 0004.\nIt emits one small k6 script per request type, scheduled by a thin main.js -- ADR 0005)
skinparam wrapWidth 200
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 16
skinparam ranksep 42

skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor<<implemented>> #d4edda
  BorderColor<<implemented>> #28a745
  BackgroundColor<<planned>> #fff3cd
  BorderColor<<planned>> #cc9a06
  BackgroundColor<<external>> #e2e3e5
  BorderColor<<external>> #6c757d
  BackgroundColor<<devonly>> #d6e9f8
  BorderColor<<devonly>> #3d7ab5
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor<<planned>> #fff3cd
  BorderColor<<planned>> #cc9a06
}
skinparam folder {
  BackgroundColor<<implemented>> #d4edda
  BorderColor<<implemented>> #28a745
}

actor "Benchmark\nEngineer" as engineer

package "Kaigara -- one repo, npm workspaces" {

  package "frontend/ (React + TypeScript + Vite)" {
    component "Connect / Load / Compose / Run\nreal data end to end" as screens <<implemented>>
    component "Analyze\nstill mock data" as analyze <<planned>>
    component "lib/api -- the ApiClient seam\nconnections / scenarios / runs are real;\nanalysis still comes from mockClient" as apiseam <<implemented>>
  }
  note right of apiseam
    In development the Vite server mounts the
    backend's **probe** and **scenario library**
    modules in-process -- both need only a socket
    and a filesystem -- so `npm run dev -w frontend`
    alone drives Connect and Load. Running a
    benchmark always needs the orchestrator.
  end note

  package "packages/shared-types/" {
    component "The metamodel\nScenario / LoadTimeline / Track / Load /\nLoadShape / RequestComposition / RequestGenerator\n+ its validator, generated JSON Schema,\nand the run wire contract" as shared <<implemented>>
  }

  package "backend/ -- Fastify orchestrator (:5174)" {
    component "REST + SSE routes\nself-documented at /swagger (OpenAPI 3.1)" as routes <<implemented>>
    component "Connection probe\nGET {baseUrl}/description, falling back\nto /shells -- standards-only" as probe <<implemented>>
    component "Scenario library\nread-only folder of documents" as library <<implemented>>
    component "RunService\norchestration, RunState projection,\nruns held in memory" as runsvc <<implemented>>
    component "Timeline compiler (k6-internal)\nLoadTimeline -> K6Plan -> one small script per\nrequest type + a thin main.js; one executor per\nLoadShape scaled by weight; compile-time\nidentifier harvest and per-script id lists" as compiler <<implemented>>
    component "Metrics aggregator\nper-second buckets + bounded latency\nreservoir; raw events never reach the UI" as aggregator <<implemented>>
    component "EngineAdapter interface\n+ registry" as adapterIface <<implemented>>
    component "k6 adapter\ncompile(timeline) -> CompiledRun,\nspawns one subprocess on main.js,\nparses --out json" as k6adapter <<implemented>>
    component "Correctness checker\najv + official JSON Schemas" as correctness <<planned>>
    component "Generated OpenAPI client\npreparation / cleanup phases" as openapiclient <<planned>>
  }

  folder "backend/scenarios/\ndemo scenario documents\n(KAIGARA_SCENARIOS_DIR)" as scenariodir <<implemented>>
  database "SQLite\nrun history, saved scenarios, connections" as sqlite <<planned>>
}

component "k6\nexternal subprocess -- AGPL,\nnever linked in-process\n(k6 run main.js)" as k6 <<external>>

package "Systems under test" {
  component "Target AAS server(s)\ntwinsphere / Eclipse BaSyx\nvia the IDTA-01002 REST API" as target <<external>>
  component "Stub AAS server\nin-memory, `npm run stub-aas` --\nwhat you aim at with no real server" as stub <<devonly>>
}

component "aas-test-engines\nofficial conformance CLI" as testengines <<external>>
component "IDTA aas-specs-api\nofficial OpenAPI spec" as idtaspec <<external>>
component "LLM backend\nhosted API or local Ollama" as llm <<external>>

engineer --> screens : composes scenarios,\nwatches runs
screens --> apiseam
analyze --> apiseam

apiseam --> routes : HTTP + SSE\nprobe, scenario library,\nrun control, live metrics
apiseam ..> shared : imports
routes ..> shared : imports
note on link
  One package, both ends -- which is why the bytes the
  Compose Code view shows are exactly the bytes
  `POST /api/runs` validates and executes. There is no
  separate export format to keep in sync.
end note

routes --> probe
routes --> library
routes --> runsvc
library --> scenariodir : reads

runsvc --> adapterIface : compile(timeline) & run
k6adapter --> compiler : validate + compile
runsvc --> aggregator : samples in, RunView out
k6adapter ..|> adapterIface : implements

k6adapter --> k6 : spawn subprocess\nwith generated scripts
k6 --> target : load generation

probe --> target : reachability +\nadvertised profiles

runsvc ..> sqlite : persist -- planned;\nruns are in-memory today
runsvc ..> correctness : pre/postcondition gates
runsvc ..> llm : scenario / instance generation\n(agreement Step 2)
correctness --> openapiclient
correctness --> testengines : shell out\n(external process)
openapiclient --> target : preparation +\ncorrectness-check calls
idtaspec ..> openapiclient : generates client\n(build-time)

note bottom of k6adapter
  Only the k6 adapter is being built within the funded
  period; further EngineAdapter implementations are
  future work, not scheduled (ADR 0001). Nothing about
  scripts, VUs or subprocesses crosses back into the
  results -- an adapter takes the authored timeline and
  emits samples; its compiled K6Plan never crosses the
  seam (ADR 0004). What it emits is many small, separately
  runnable scripts scheduled by a thin main.js (ADR 0005).
  A second engine brings its own compiler.
end note

note bottom of runsvc
  **Not implemented:** the preparation, preconditions,
  postconditions and cleanup phases. Only `method` runs;
  the other four report `skipped` rather than `done`, so
  a clean run is never mistaken for "correctness checks
  passed".
end note

legend right
  |     | Status |
  |<#d4edda>| Implemented |
  |<#fff3cd>| Proposed, not yet built |
  |<#d6e9f8>| Development convenience only |
  |<#e2e3e5>| External tool / third-party system |
endlegend

@enduml
